      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/plato#MetaTypeScheme"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/plato#ContainedIn",
    "@type": [
      "https://w3id.org/plato#RelationType",
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n        The subject SpatialEntity is contained in the target SpatialEntity, for\n        the attested timespan: a parish in a hundred, a hundred in a county.\n        Not an identity relation and not fixed by the class model; it is a\n        claim, with a source and a certainty, like any other attestation.\n\n        When a dataset's containing regions are matched to a gazetteer (a\n        parish's county and country, looked up level by level), two claims\n        are made, and kept apart. The dataset's own claim is ContainedIn,\n        pointing at a region minted from the dataset itself, one for each\n        full chain of containers (England, Surrey), never for the name\n        alone, so that two regions with one name in different chains are not\n        merged. The reviewer's decision that this region is the gazetteer's is\n        an IdentityRelation from it, whose promoted_from names the Candidate\n        that holds the matching software's similarity_score. A match score is\n        not a certainty, so it is never put on the containment. In Linked\n        Places Format the two are written together as one\n        gvp:broaderPartitive relation: its relationTo is the identity's\n        object, its certainty the identity attestation's certainty level, its\n        whg_match_score the Candidate's score and its label the region's\n        name. A region assigned by hand, with no software suggestion, may be\n        stated directly against the gazetteer's address instead.\n    "
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/plato"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso": [
      {
        "@id": "http://vocab.getty.edu/ontology#broaderPartitive"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The subject SpatialEntity is contained in the target SpatialEntity, for the attested timespan: a parish in a hundred, a hundred in a county. Not an identity relation and not fixed by the class model; it is a claim, with a source and a certainty, like any other attestation. When a dataset's containing regions are matched to a gazetteer (a parish's county and country, looked up level by level), two claims are made, and kept apart. The dataset's own claim is ContainedIn, pointing at a region minted from the dataset itself, one for each full chain of containers (England, Surrey), never for the name alone, so that two regions with one name in different chains are not merged. The reviewer's decision that this region is the gazetteer's is an IdentityRelation from it, whose promoted_from names the Candidate that holds the matching software's similarity_score. A match score is not a certainty, so it is never put on the containment. In Linked Places Format the two are written together as one gvp:broaderPartitive relation: its relationTo is the identity's object, its certainty the identity attestation's certainty level, its whg_match_score the Candidate's score and its label the region's name. A region assigned by hand, with no software suggestion, may be stated directly against the gazetteer's address instead."
      }
    ],
